# Build context exclusions for backend/Dockerfile.
#
# There is a specific incident behind this file. With no .dockerignore, `COPY . .`
# baked the developer's own rag/chroma_db into the image — which is where
# "Vector store initialized with 49 existing docs" came from on a container that
# had never ingested anything. Now that the index is a named volume, that is
# worse than untidy: Docker seeds a new named volume from whatever the image has
# at the mount point, so a stale or zero-vector-poisoned index would reappear
# after every rebuild and survive `docker compose down -v`.
#
# It also cut a 26MB build context (20MB of it one developer's checkpoints.db)
# down to the source that actually needs to ship.

# --- Runtime state: belongs on a volume, never in an image layer -------------
rag/chroma_db/
memory/*.db
memory/*.db-shm
memory/*.db-wal
data/

# Fetched reference docs are a cache the container rebuilds over plain HTTP.
# Unchanged docs hash to ids the index already holds, so this costs no quota.
rag/reference/**/_fetched/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The root .env reaches the container through compose's env_file at run time.
# A key copied into a layer stays in that layer forever, whatever deletes it later.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- Build and test detritus -------------------------------------------------
# Stale .pyc compiled by a different interpreter than the image's python:3.12
# is actively harmful, not merely large.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
